  <header class="top"><div class="shell top-inner"><a class="brand" href="index.php"><span>L</span>LChat</a><nav><a href="index.php">Open messenger</a><a href="#methods">API methods</a></nav></div></header>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Developer documentation</div><h1>LChat Bot API</h1><p>Create a bot with <strong>@BotCreator</strong>, get an API token, and respond to messages from a PHP script or any other server.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="index.php">Find @BotCreator →</a><a class="button secondary" href="#quickstart">Quick start</a></div></section>
    <div class="layout"><aside class="toc"><b>Contents</b><a href="#quickstart">Quick start</a><a href="#creator">BotCreator commands</a><a href="#auth">Authentication</a><a href="#methods">API methods</a><a href="#keyboards">Keyboards</a><a href="#examples">Examples</a><a href="#limits">Delivery and limits</a></aside><main class="content">
      <section id="quickstart" class="section"><h2>Quick start</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Sign in to LChat and search for <strong>@BotCreator</strong>, or open <strong>🤖 My bots → Message @BotCreator</strong>.</li><li>Send <code>/newbot</code>, then choose a display name and an available username ending in <code>bot</code>.</li><li>Copy the token from the response. Call <code>getMe</code> to verify it.</li><li>Open a private chat with the bot, or add it to a group or channel you own. The bot then receives new messages through <code>getUpdates</code> or a webhook.</li></ol><p class="note">A token grants access to the bot account. Keep it on your server; do not put it in HTML or browser JavaScript.</p></section>
      <section id="creator" class="section"><h2>@BotCreator</h2><p>BotCreator is a built-in LChat account. Send commands as regular messages in a private chat. No separate bot password is needed.</p><div class="commands"><code>/start</code><span>Show the welcome message and commands.</span><code>/newbot</code><span>Create a bot and receive an API token.</span><code>/mybots</code><span>List your bots.</span><code>/token @helperbot</code><span>Rotate the token. The previous token stops working immediately.</span><code>/setname @helperbot New name</code><span>Change the bot display name.</span><code>/cancel</code><span>Cancel bot creation.</span></div><p>Each user can create up to 10 bots. Usernames start with a Latin letter, contain Latin letters, digits, or underscores, and end in <code>bot</code>.</p></section>
      <section id="auth" class="section"><h2>Authentication and response format</h2><p>Base endpoint: <code>https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=METHOD</code>. Send the token in <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN</code> or <code>X-LChat-Bot-Token</code>. The short URL <code>https://chat.lbs.su/bot&lt;TOKEN&gt;/&lt;METHOD&gt;</code> is also supported when Apache rewrite rules are enabled.</p><p>Responses are JSON: <code>{"ok":true,"result":...}</code> or <code>{"ok":false,"error_code":400,"description":"..."}</code>. Send methods accept JSON or form fields.</p></section>
      <section id="methods" class="section"><h2>API methods</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>HTTP</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>getMe</code>, <code>getChat</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Read bot and accessible chat information.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getUpdates</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Get messages and button callbacks; accepts <code>offset</code> and <code>limit</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>setWebhook</code>, <code>deleteWebhook</code>, <code>getWebhookInfo</code></td><td>POST / GET</td><td>Configure, disable, or inspect an HTTPS webhook.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sendMessage</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Send text with optional inline buttons or a reply keyboard.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sendDocument</code>, <code>sendPhoto</code>, <code>sendAudio</code>, <code>sendVideo</code>, <code>sendVoice</code>, <code>sendAnimation</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Send a multipart upload or an accessible <code>file_id</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getFile</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Read file metadata and its download path.</td></tr><tr><td><code>editMessageText</code>, <code>editMessageReplyMarkup</code>, <code>deleteMessage</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Edit the bot message or its buttons; delete a bot message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>answerCallbackQuery</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Acknowledge an inline button press.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>With <code>getUpdates</code>, set <code>offset</code> to the last <code>update_id + 1</code> and use <code>limit</code> from 1 to 100. Store the offset in your bot process. Polling is disabled while a webhook is active.</p></section>
      <section id="keyboards" class="section"><h2>Bot keyboards</h2><p>For inline buttons, put <code>inline_keyboard</code> in <code>reply_markup</code>. Buttons may contain an HTTPS <code>url</code> or <code>callback_data</code>. Answer callback updates with <code>answerCallbackQuery</code>.</p><pre>{"inline_keyboard":[[{"text":"Done","callback_data":"done"},{"text":"Website","url":"https://example.com"}]]}</pre><p>For a keyboard above the message field, use <code>keyboard</code>. Pressing a button sends its text to the bot. You can set <code>resize_keyboard</code>, <code>one_time_keyboard</code>, and <code>input_field_placeholder</code>. Send <code>{"remove_keyboard":true}</code> to hide it.</p><pre>{"keyboard":[[{"text":"Help"},{"text":"Profile"}]],"resize_keyboard":true}</pre></section>
      <section id="examples" class="section"><h2>Examples</h2><h3>Verify the token</h3><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=getMe"</pre><h3>Read updates</h3><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=getUpdates&amp;offset=0"</pre><h3>Send a message</h3><pre>curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"chat_id":123,"text":"Hello!"}' "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=sendMessage"</pre><h3>Send a file</h3><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" -F "chat_id=123" -F "document=@photo.png" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=sendDocument"</pre><p>Take <code>chat_id</code> from <code>message.chat.id</code> in a <code>getUpdates</code> response. Poll with a delay between requests.</p></section>
      <section id="limits" class="section"><h2>Delivery and limits</h2><p>Bots see only new messages in chats they have joined. Use short polling with <code>getUpdates</code>, or set a public HTTPS endpoint with <code>setWebhook</code>. Webhooks send JSON by cURL after a site request. To retry delivery without new site traffic, run <code>php tools/bot-webhook-worker.php</code> with cron. Validate the <code>X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token</code> header when using a secret token.</p><p>Files can be up to 8 MB; bot storage is limited to 200 MB. The listed methods are implemented, but this is not a complete Telegram Bot API implementation: payments, stickers, and many other methods are unavailable. Old messages are not replayed after the update queue is initialized.</p></section>
    </main></div>
